@startuml BitePlate_DerivedFromSnippet
title Code-to-Diagram Derivation — Reverse-Engineered UML Class Diagram

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontSize 13
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam classBorderColor #444444
skinparam classBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam arrowColor #444444
skinparam arrowThickness 1.5
skinparam padding 6

abstract class "AbstractSubject\n<<Subject>>" as AS {
  # listeners : List<Listener>
  + add(l : Listener) : void
  + notifyAll(event : Object) : void
}

class "ConcreteSubject\n<<ConcreteSubject>>" as CS {
  - state : String
  + ConcreteSubject()
  + setState(s : String) : void
}

interface "Listener\n<<Observer>>" as L {
  + onEvent(event : Object) : void
}

class "ConcreteListenerA\n<<ConcreteObserver>>" as CLA {
  + onEvent(event : Object) : void
}

class "ConcreteListenerB\n<<ConcreteObserver>>" as CLB {
  + onEvent(event : Object) : void
}

AS <|-- CS
L <|.. CLA
L <|.. CLB

AS o-- L : listeners\n0..*

note top of AS
  Abstract base class identified from 'abstract' keyword (snippet line 1).
  Protected collection modelled as aggregation:
  listeners exist independently of the subject.
end note

note right of CS
  Calls super() in constructor (snippet line 8).
  setState() calls notifyAll() internally —
  inferred from the loop in notifyAll() firing after
  each state mutation in the snippet.
end note

note bottom of CLA
  Registers via subject.add(this) (snippet line 22).
  Loop in notifyAll() fires onEvent() on each element.
  Pattern identified: Observer (Gamma et al., 1994).
  Assumption: protected field intended for subclass extension —
  had it been private with a getter, relationship
  would be modelled as composition instead.
end note

@enduml